WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
Fixing notes
Change, move, delete and enter single notes, without recording again.

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:11.760
1. Open Notes
Press PLAY. On the Band page, turn ALGORITHM to BA for the bass, then press SEQ.

3
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:19.160
2. Pick a note
Turn SELECT. It steps from note to note, and the line at the top names it.

4
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:24.240
3. Change its pitch
Turn KNOB 2 (Pitch) one step. On this note the bass always plays the chord's root, so Polly asks.

5
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:30.220
3. Change its pitch
Press SEL for yes, and the bass plays your notes as written. Keep turning to E2.

6
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:37.000
4. Change its length and velocity
Turn KNOB 3 (Length) to make it longer, and KNOB 4 (Velocity) to make it softer.

7
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:43.804
5. Move it
Hold SEL and turn SELECT. The note moves one grid step for each click of the knob.

8
00:00:43.804 --> 00:00:48.884
6. Delete a note, enter one
Press EDIT to delete the selected note.

9
00:00:48.884 --> 00:00:56.088
6. Delete a note, enter one
Turn KNOB 1 (Place) to an empty place, then play a key. The note goes in there.

10
00:00:56.088 --> 00:01:03.472
7. Undo
Hold HOME and press REC. Your last edit is undone, and the header tells you what changed.

11
00:01:03.472 --> 00:01:07.352
7. Undo
Press PLAY to stop.

12
00:01:07.352 --> 00:01:11.400
Next: 108
Making it sound yours.
